    "summary_insights": [
      "Revenue growth is marginal at +1.9%, constrained by regulatory approval delays under the UK Building Safety Act.",
      "Gross margin has compressed from 37.8% to 35.2%, driven by a 6.3% increase in Cost of Sales that outpaced turnover growth.",
      "Operating expenses rose significantly by 17.5% (£722k), primarily due to £200k investment in AI systems and headcount expansion for FY27 scaling.",
      "Statutory EBITDA declined by 38.3% and Net Profit fell by 40.3%, reflecting the combined impact of margin pressure and heavy overhead investment.",
      "The company maintains a very strong liquidity position with a current ratio improving from 2.78x to 4.44x and negligible long-term debt.",
      "Interest coverage has improved dramatically as financial debt was significantly reduced, leaving the balance sheet materially cash-positive.",
      "A new D2C division, Lurano, was successfully launched in FY26, contributing £159k in its first year.",
      "Management attributes the current profit decline to a 'transition year' of infrastructure investment ahead of anticipated volume scaling in FY27."
    ]
  },
